  message: "DONE, merged as PR #571 (33550c62eb). 24 rows across std::process and std::env;\nstd::thread ruled ABSENT ENTIRELY. Evidence re-run on the MERGED tree: the\nitem's own 45 tests pass, catalogue loads at 169 rows, and the starvation\ncontrol in the same run is unchanged (9 of 42 surveys starve; std::path::Path\nin 3 of 3 rust repos, exactly as before).\n\nTHIS ITEM'S ROWS FIRE, WHICH NO EARLIER ITEM IN THE ARC COULD SAY. Measured\nA/B on the 42-repo cohort with the production loader and production classifier:\nstd::env::temp_dir NEWLY CLASSIFIES 3 EDGES as host_info_read (ripgrep 2,\ny-sweet 1). Small, and stated as small -- but it is the first row of this arc to\nmove an edge at all, and it CONFIRMS rather than contradicts WI-gihos: function\n-kind rows match, method-kind rows cannot (INV-linub L3/L4). The std::process\nMETHOD rows are therefore inert today, said here rather than found later. The\nitem's PAY EXPECTATION (\"no verdict moves on either testable rust repo\") holds:\n3 edges classified is not a verdict change.\n\nBOUNDARIES TAKEN FROM python.yaml, NOT CHOSEN: putenv/unsetenv/chdir -> env_write\n(rust's FIRST env_write section: set_var, remove_var, set_current_dir);\nos.kill -> ipc_send (Child::kill); os.wait/waitpid -> ipc_recv\n(Child::{wait,try_wait,wait_with_output}); tempfile.gettempdir ->\nhost_info_read (temp_dir, home_dir). vars_os added under env_read as the\nOsString peer of vars. ChildStdin/ChildStdout/ChildStderr carry their trait\nmethods ON THE CONCRETE TYPE per WI-gihos's keying rule. `set_current_dir` was\nPROMISED IN ADVANCE by rust.yaml's own note (\"chdir has no row here: python\nrules it env_write, and rust's std::env::set_current_dir is not yet audited\").\n\nTHE RULING THIS ITEM WAS FILED TO MAKE -- std::thread is ABSENT ENTIRELY.\nThe item asked whether std::thread's internal RUST_MIN_STACK read makes\nthread::spawn an env_read boundary for a caller who never names a variable.\nNO. The deciding reason is DISCRIMINATION, not precedent: the read is INTERNAL,\nit sizes the new thread's stack, and its value never reaches the caller. If\nthat counted, locale lookups, TZ, RUST_BACKTRACE and a long tail of stdlib\nmachinery would all qualify, and env_read would stop distinguishing \"this code\nreads configuration\" from \"this code runs on a stdlib that does\". A BOUNDARY\nTHAT EVERYTHING SATISFIES CLASSIFIES NOTHING. Supporting, weaker: rust.yaml\nalready declared concurrency primitives absent, and the owner's boundary test\n(\"is it changing state outside of itself\") puts a thread inside the process,\nas WI-pavob applied to locks. PYTHON IS SILENT HERE, NOT SUPPORTIVE --\n`threading` appears only in python.yaml's stdlib_modules NAME LIST, with no\nrows and no completeness entry -- and I am recording that as silence rather\nthan dressing it up as agreement (LIVE.md rule 7). REVERSIBLE: if a repository\nis ever found whose behaviour genuinely turns on RUST_MIN_STACK, reopen this.\n\nA FOURTH PROBE BUG, and the first to hit a KIND rather than a name. The\nreceiver regex required a leading `&`, so `fn wait_with_output(mut self)` and\n46 OTHER by-value receivers in process.rs read as ASSOCIATED FUNCTIONS. Kind is\nexactly what decides matchability, so that would have shipped a function-kind\nrow no method call could ever match (INV-nular). Caught by disbelieving an\nimplausible intermediate, not by an error. Since the same enumerator produced\nWI-gihos's rows, I re-checked all 70 already-merged ones: NONE affected, because\nthe by-value names there (by_ref, bytes, chain, take) were refused as adapters.\n\nREFUSALS, each with a reason and a test: std::process::id and Child::id (python\ndeliberately holds os.getpid out); Command's builder setters (they mutate a\nbuilder in THIS process; spawn is already rowed -- WI-bupor's OpenOptionsExt\nrule); ExitStatus accessors; Stdio constructors; join_paths/split_paths (pure\nOsString manipulation); thread::available_parallelism (python holds\nos.cpu_count out for the same reason it holds getpid out).\n\nFILED, NOT CHASED: python.yaml's tempfile completeness entry says \"gettempdir\nrowed under env_read\" while the row sits under host_info_read -- a note that\npredates the INV-tutar split. Worth a line in the next catalogue sweep."  # c166
